Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.31 auto-save: load baseline and title start notes

P6.31 Auto-save: STGMCARD_loadSave (after a successful load of a card slot)
tells the port (dw3_autosave_note_loaded) so the loaded area is the baseline:
loading is not an area change. The title menu's task start (new game, load,
return to title) calls dw3_autosave_title_started, which forgets the baseline
and looks at autosave.bin again for the Continue / Load rows (patch 0142).
Both calls do nothing with the option OFF and no auto-save file.

--- a/src/menus/memory_card/saves.c
+++ b/src/menus/memory_card/saves.c
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 #include "menus/memory_card.h"
 #if PORT_HOST
 #include <stdio.h>
+#include "port_autosave.h"
 char *getenv(const char *name);
 #ifdef DW3_CHEATS
 #include "port_cheats.h"
@@ -475,6 +476,8 @@
                 dw3_cheats_save_loaded(saves->port, STGMCARD_funcs.slot, STGMCARD_funcs.dataBuf->bytes,
                                        sizeof(GameSave));
 #endif
+                /* P6.31: loading is not an area change (auto-save baseline) */
+                dw3_autosave_note_loaded();
                 if (getenv("DW3_FORCE_MCARD_LOAD") != NULL) {
                     fprintf(stderr, "dw3: STGMCARD force-load done, leaving\n");
                     saves->hide(saves);
